# Cursor Rules for DocuMorph
# See full engineering standards and architectural rules in GEMINI.md

Please follow all instructions defined in GEMINI.md:
- Feature-driven folder structure (src/features/<feature>/)
- Separate business logic from UI components via custom hooks and services
- Remove duplicate and dead code
- Use consistent naming conventions (PascalCase components, camelCase functions/hooks)
- Robust error handling with user-facing fallbacks
- Separate environment configs via Zod schema (zero hardcoded secrets)
- Modular reusable components (< 250 lines)
- Predictable Zustand state management without cascading useEffect setStates
- Document codebase with TSDoc and maintain ARCHITECTURE.md & AGENTS.md
- Scalable versioned API routes with standard response envelope
- Runtime validation with Zod
- Verification gates: ensure `pnpm tsc --noEmit && pnpm lint && pnpm build` pass cleanly
